Search for three questions your customers commonly ask, in ChatGPT or Perplexity. Notice which sources are cited. Are any your competitors? Is your brand cited anywhere? Now check whether your top content pages have: (a) FAQ sections with direct answers, (b) Schema markup, and (c) content that answers the question in the first sentence. This gap analysis tells you exactly where to start your GEO work.


Chapter 5: Content Marketing
📖 Chapter Overview
Content marketing is the practice of creating and distributing valuable content to attract, engage, and retain a defined audience — with the long-term goal of building trust that converts to business outcomes. It is not about producing content for content's sake. It is about creating material that your audience actually wants to consume, that demonstrates your expertise, and that positions your brand as the natural choice when they are ready to buy. This chapter covers content strategy, formats, distribution, AI-assisted creation, and how to measure whether your content is working.


5.1 Content Strategy
Strategy is what separates content marketing from content production. Without a strategy, you produce content that satisfies the editorial calendar but does not serve the business. A content strategy starts with three questions:
Who is the content for? (Target persona and their stage in the customer journey)
What problem does it solve for them? (Genuine value, not brand promotion)
How does it move them closer to a business outcome? (The connection to revenue)

The Topic Cluster Model
A topic cluster is a content architecture built around one 'pillar' page (a comprehensive overview of a broad topic) supported by multiple cluster pages (deep dives into specific subtopics) that link back to the pillar. This structure improves SEO authority for the entire topic area and guides users through a logical content journey.
💡 Topic Cluster Example
Pillar page: 'The Complete Guide to Email Marketing'
Cluster pages: 'How to Write Email Subject Lines,' 'Email Segmentation Best Practices,' 'Email Automation Workflows,' 'Email Deliverability Explained,' 'How to Build an Email List.'
Each cluster page links back to the pillar. The pillar links out to each cluster. Google recognises this as topical authority — and ranks the entire cluster higher than isolated pages would rank.


