Chapter 6: Social Media Marketing
📖 Chapter Overview
Social media is the most visible layer of most brands' marketing — and the most misunderstood. It is not just a content distribution channel. It is a community platform, a research tool, a customer service interface, a commerce layer, and a crisis management arena. This chapter covers platform strategy, content by platform, influencer marketing, social commerce, and crisis communication — because a brand that has not prepared for a social media crisis is not managing social media, it is hoping.


6.1 Platform Strategy
The most expensive social media mistake is trying to be everywhere. Every platform requires a different content format, different posting cadence, different community management approach, and different creative style. Spreading thin across six platforms produces mediocre performance on all of them.
Platform selection should follow your audience: be present where your specific customer segments actually spend their time, and invest deeply there before expanding. A B2B company's ideal customer probably spends more time on LinkedIn than TikTok, even if TikTok has more users.

